# Session context envelope (Cursor)

**THIS SURFACE IS CURSOR — use `.cursor/` only for rules/MCP config.**

| You | Primary |
|-----|---------|
| **Cursor** | **`.cursor/`** · `.cursor/project-manifest.yaml` · `.cursor/rules/` · `.cursor/mcp.json` |
| Not primary | `.grok/`, `.claude/`, `.github/skills/`, `.copilot/`, `.gemini/` |

Shared OK: `TODO/`, `docs/`, `scripts/`, `reports/`. Map: `docs/reference/platform-surfaces.md`.

At session start:

```bash
python3 scripts/session-context-envelope.py --write
```

- Print the compact CTX block (do not restate in long prose).
- Honor `surface root=.cursor` for Cursor-specific rules; do not prefer other platform skill trees.
- **Always surface `ask:` / pickup** so the user can continue last work if they wish. Never auto-checkout.
- Surface **`ws primary=…`** when present (multi-workstream — `.cursor/rules/multi-workstream.mdc`).
- Warn when `behind_develop>0` before release/version work.
- MCP is develop-only (local DDEV / Docker / host stdio — never public hosts).
- If `identity≠ok`, do not trust manifest stack/runtime until customized.

See `docs/reference/session-context-token-budget.md`.
